## USER ROLES (4 personas — always code with these in mind)
1. **Турист** — short stay, needs tours, transfers, experiences
2. **Резидент** — expat living in Phuket, needs household services, delivery, repairs
3. **Собственник** — property owner, needs property management, rental income tracking
4. **Инвестор** — HNWI, needs real estate deals, ROI data, market analytics

## ARCHITECTURE RULES
- Always use APP_ROUTES constants for navigation — never hardcode paths
- Supabase client is initialized once — import from existing client file, never create new instances
- All API calls must have error handling and loading states
- Use existing component patterns before creating new ones — check /src/components first
- Prefer composition over creating large monolithic components
- Keep business logic in hooks (/src/hooks), not in components

## CODE QUALITY
- TypeScript strict mode — avoid `any`, use proper types
- No console.log in production code — use proper error boundaries
- All user-facing text must support Russian and English (i18n-ready)
- Mobile-first responsive design — primary users are on phones
- Performance: use React.lazy for route-level code splitting

## SUPABASE PATTERNS
- Always use Row Level Security (RLS) — never bypass it
- Use Supabase realtime for live updates where appropriate
- Edge functions for sensitive business logic (payments, OTA sync)
- Never expose service role key in frontend code

## BUSINESS LOGIC PRIORITIES (in order)
1. User onboarding and role selection (Турист/Резидент/Собственник/Инвестор)
2. Service catalog and booking flow
3. Vendor/provider management
4. Payment processing
5. Property owner dashboard
6. Investor analytics

## WHEN ADDING FEATURES — ALWAYS ASK:
- Which of the 4 user personas does this serve?
- Does this move myUNO toward first 100 real transactions?
- Is there an existing component/hook/utility to reuse?
- Does this work on mobile?

## CURRENT PRIORITIES (focus here first)
- Stability over new features
- Fix existing bugs before adding new functionality
- Every feature needs a working happy path before edge cases
- Real data flows over mock/placeholder data

## LANGUAGE
- UI strings: Russian primary, English secondary
- Code, comments, variable names: English only
- Commit messages: English

## DO NOT
- Do not create duplicate Supabase client instances
- Do not hardcode route strings — use APP_ROUTES
- Do not add dependencies without checking if existing ones cover the need
- Do not remove existing error handling
- Do not make breaking changes to database schema without migration files
- Do not skip TypeScript types — no implicit any

## DEPLOYMENT
- main branch = production (auto-deploys to Vercel)
- Always test locally with `npm run dev` before pushing
- Run `npm run build` to check for build errors before `git push`
